Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg
Use FTDashIcons.pkg
Use cFTLibraryReport.pkg
Use FTMarkupBuilders.pkg         // the HTML vocabulary - OpenHtml, IconLabel, the builders
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg      // CS_DivEnd / CS_UpTriangle and the other named glyphs

/*  cFTTileMarkup - the cockpit tiles that BOTH boards paint: Workspace, Target DataFlex version,
    Modernization progress, and the utility action row.

    LIFTED OUT OF THE DASHBOARD VIEW (2026-07-31), third and last slice of the untangle. These four
    are pure builders - they read ghoApplication and return HTML, touching no view state at all -
    but they lived inside oDashboard_vw, so the guided trail had to reach INTO a sibling view to
    paint its own tiles: SetupTileHtml(oDashboard_vw(hoDash)). One screen could not be changed
    without the other, and neither could be retired.

    Now both boards call the same handle and neither knows the other exists. That is the whole
    point of the slice: the Dashboard becomes an ordinary screen, free to have tiles stripped out
    of it without the trail going dark.

    The tooltips travel with the markup they are spliced into (they are arguments to these
    builders, not the view's own text); the tips for tiles that stayed behind stayed with them.
    Same no-double-quote rule as ever - a double quote would close both the Define and the HTML
    title attribute it lands in.
*/
Define CS_WorkspaceTileTip  for "The DataFlex workspace (.sws) DFRefactor will operate on - required before any refactoring. Click to choose one, or pick a recent below."
Define CS_SetupTileTip      for "The DataFlex version the code is moving to. DFRefactor compiles with that version and knows which old commands it no longer supports, so the warnings and suggested fixes are for that version, not for the one the code was written for. Click to change."
Define CS_ProgressTileTip   for "Modernization burn-down: how compiler warnings, scan findings, errors and analyzer auto-fixes have fallen across the cycles. Warnings and findings are counted apart - the compiler never reports what a source scan finds - and the findings count appears only once a cycle has any. Click to open the full history and trend, or reset the counter for a fresh baseline."
// The Check row, on both boards. Long prose belongs beside the other tip constants rather than
// inside a markup string - these are the strings most likely to be re-read and re-worded, and
// buried in a span they are the hardest in the app to find.
Define CS_AdjustFoldersTip  for "Choose which folders the source analyze and the manual passes cover. The compile half of a Check always follows the selected program instead, whatever is picked here."
Define CS_AnalyzeRulesTip   for "Choose which obsolete symbols the source analyze searches for. Changing them makes the next Check re-scan from scratch."
Define CS_ActStartTip       for "Runs the selected refactoring functions now, on the selected source folders or on the loaded file. Same as Start Refactoring on the toolbar (Ctrl+F5)."
Define CS_ActLogTip         for "Open the run summary log file DFRefactor appends to after each refactoring run."
Define CS_ActOtherTip       for "View the list of log files produced by eOther_Function refactors."
Define CS_ActCompareTip     for "Compare the before/after of the last refactoring run in your external file-compare tool (e.g. Beyond Compare)."
Define CS_ActUndoTip        for "Open the Undo Refactoring dialog to restore files from the DFRefactor backup folder."

// Disabled-state (ENABLING) tips for the action-row chips - a grey chip explains what lights it rather
// than repeating what it would do. Run Refactoring builds its disabled tip DYNAMICALLY in
// ActionRowHtml (it names the specific missing ingredient); these cover the static gates.
Define CS_ActPlanOffTip     for "No saved Modernization plan yet - run the guided flow first: click Create Modernization Plan above to compile, analyze and build one."
Define CS_ActLogOffTip      for "No run summary log yet - it is written by the first refactoring run."
Define CS_ActOtherOffTip    for "No eOther_Function logs yet - some refactoring functions write one when they run."
Define CS_ActCompareOffTip  for "Nothing to compare yet - a refactoring run first has to create backups of the files it changes."
Define CS_ActUndoOffTip     for "Nothing to revert - no refactoring run has created backups for this workspace yet."

Define CS_BackupCycleTip    for "DFRefactor keeps the FIRST backup of a file untouched for the whole overwrite cycle, so Undo Refactoring means 'back to how it was before I started'. Once a file's source is more than that many days newer than its backup, the next run backs it up again - replacing the pristine original with source that has already been refactored. AMBER means that has already happened and the next run does the overwriting; the quieter state means the backups are simply older than the cycle, so they survive the next run but any file it changes is overwritten by the run after. Raise the cycle on the Settings dialog, or copy the backup folder aside, to keep the originals."

Define CS_StatsTileTip      for "How many refactoring functions DFRefactor offers in each group (Modernization, x64 + Unicode, Tidy Up, Other) - the size of the toolbox, independent of your selection. Click a group figure to open the function library filtered to that group; click Total (or the title) for all groups."

Class cFTTileMarkup is a cObject

    /* The .sws basename without its extension - the name a person calls their workspace.

       Extracted 2026-08-09, when the trail's scope band needed it and would have made a FOURTH
       copy: this class already derived it twice (the banner headline and the crumb), and
       StartCenterFT.vw kept a third as ScWsName until 2026-10-10. Same six lines every time, so
       any fix to how a name is derived - a UNC path, a workspace with a dot in its name - had
       three places to miss; the Start Center asks here now.

       Defined at the top of the class because every caller here is below it and function-style
       calls resolve at compile time. */
    Function WorkspaceShortName String sPath Returns String
        String sName
        Integer iPos
        Move (RightPos("\", sPath)) to iPos
        If (iPos > 0) ;
            Move (Right(sPath, (Length(sPath) - iPos))) to sName
        Else ;
            Move sPath to sName
        Move (RightPos(".", sName)) to iPos
        If (iPos > 1) ;
            Move (Left(sName, (iPos - 1))) to sName
        Function_Return sName
    End_Function

    /* THE WORKSPACE CRUMB - what a board carries in place of the tile above (Nils 2026-08-06).

       The Start Center owns workspace selection now, so the boards give the tile up. That trade
       leaves a hole the crumb exists to fill: without it a board would show neither which .sws is
       loaded, nor its path, nor any route to a different one - the tile was the only affordance
       for all three. DF 26's Studio hit exactly this when it split Start Center from Workspace
       Dashboard, and answered it with a toggle (its command 705); this is the same answer in one
       line: it names where you are and it is the way back.

       It also carries the LANE SWITCH by implication - going back is how you take the other door.

       ONE data-ServerOnClick, on the back link ALONE. The row is not clickable: a click anywhere
       on a cWebHtmlBox fires every ancestor's handler, and a whole-width click target that
       navigates away from a board mid-work is exactly the sort of accident the boards' own click
       isolation is written to prevent. Both boards route the "startcenter" id to their own timer.

       The backup-cycle warning deliberately does NOT ride along: it belonged to the workspace tile
       and it is a paragraph, not a crumb. (That tile went with WorkspaceTileHtml, removed
       2026-08-25 - its only caller was the Dashboard retired on 08-10.) */
    /* THE CRUMB CARRIES ITS OWN CSS (Nils 2026-08-06, when Select Folders joined the callers).

       The two boards host their tiles in a cDbLocalWebControlHost, where application.css reaches
       them - that is why every .dash-* class works there with no inline style. Select Folders uses
       a plain cLocalWebControlHost, and EVERY tile in every one of those (TestCompileFT's .tcbtn,
       this view's own .sfbtn, ModProgressHistoryFT...) inlines its own rules
       instead. Not one of them relies on application.css for a custom class.

       Rather than keep a second copy of these rules for the odd host out - the exact drift this
       shared builder exists to prevent - the markup now ships the style with it. One definition,
       correct in either host, and no caller had to change. The .dash-crumb block was removed from
       application.css in the same edit; if it ever reappears there, one of them is dead. */
    /* AMBER, not the mint the links wore until 2026-08-12 (Nils: "the text can be a bit difficult
       to find/read"). var(--dfr-amber, #e6a571) is the palette's established amber - the same hue .dash-tile.t-modernize
       and the Run Modernization Plan chip wear - so the crumb reads as a live control against the
       var(--dfr-bg-card, #2c2b29) card rather than as quiet decoration. The FORWARD twin moves with it: the note on
       .dash-crumb-fwd below is explicit that a breadcrumb names places at both ends with ONE link
       treatment, and leaving one mint would break exactly that. Hover tint follows the same colour
       at the same .12 alpha (230,165,113). */
    Function WorkspaceCrumbCss Returns String
        String s
        Move (CS_PaletteCssLink + CssLink("tilemarkup")) to s
        Function_Return s
    End_Function

    /* The crumb with an optional FORWARD link at the far end, so a screen that has a next step can
       state it in the same breadcrumb rather than beside one (Nils 2026-08-06: "make it a bread
       crumb, like the Start Center one").

       sTail is markup, not a caption, because only the caller knows what its next step is called
       and which id it routes to - Select Folders passes a "Select Functions" link, the boards pass
       nothing. It goes INSIDE the .dash-crumb row, which is the whole point: a sibling div would
       land on its own line and be a second bar. */
    /* THE CRUMB'S ROOT - what "back" means on the screen painting it (Nils 2026-08-09: "if one of
       the dashboards have been selected, it would probably be more logical to return to the current
       dashboard?").

       bFollowSurface False is the BOARDS' answer and never changes: a board's parent IS the Start
       Center, so its crumb roots there whatever piLastSurface says.

       True is for the screens hanging off a surface - Select Folders and Select Functions - which
       are reached from the Start Center AND from any of the three boards. Sending someone back to
       the Start Center after they stepped in from a board is the losing-your-place complaint the
       guided flow exists to fix; sending them to a board they never opened would be the same
       mistake pointing the other way, which is why this reads piLastSurface and not
       piLastBoardView (see the eSurfaceStartCenter comment in RefactorConstants.h.pkg).

       The LABEL follows the target rather than staying "Start Center". A breadcrumb whose root
       names one screen and lands on another is not a shortened path, it is a wrong one - and the
       root is the only part of this crumb that says where back goes.

       Only the non-Start-Center roots carry the new "crumbroot" id; the Start Center keeps
       "startcenter", so every existing handler still works untouched. Defined above its callers -
       function-style calls resolve at compile time. */
    Function CrumbRootHtml Boolean bFollowSurface Returns String
        Integer iSurface
        Move eSurfaceStartCenter to iSurface
        If (bFollowSurface = True) ;
            Get piLastSurface of ghoApplication to iSurface
        If (iSurface = eBoardGuided) ;
            Function_Return ((ClickableHtml("span", "dash-crumb-back dash-crumb-g", "crumbroot", "", ((DashIcon(CS_GlyphChevron)) + 'Guided Dashboard'), "Back to the guided dashboard you stepped in from.")))
        If (iSurface = eBoardManual) ;
            Function_Return ((ClickableHtml("span", "dash-crumb-back dash-crumb-m", "crumbroot", "", ((DashIcon(CS_GlyphChevron)) + 'Manual Dashboard'), "Back to the manual dashboard you stepped in from.")))
        If (iSurface = eBoardCockpit) ;
            Function_Return ((ClickableHtml("span", "dash-crumb-back dash-crumb-g", "crumbroot", "", ((DashIcon(CS_GlyphChevron)) + 'Dashboard'), "Back to the dashboard you stepped in from.")))
        Function_Return ((ClickableHtml("span", "dash-crumb-back", "startcenter", "", ((DashIcon(CS_GlyphChevron)) + 'Start Center'), "Back to the Start Center, to open another workspace or to switch between the guided and manual dashboards.")))
    End_Function

    // The crumb with its root supplied - the one body both roots share, so the workspace name, the
    // no-workspace case and the tail slot can never drift between them.
    Function WorkspaceCrumbRootTailHtml String sRoot String sTail Returns String
        String sWS sName sPath

        Get psSWSFile of ghoApplication to sWS
        Move ((WorkspaceCrumbCss(Self)) + (DivOpen("dash-crumb")) + sRoot + (((SpanOpen("dash-crumb-sep")) + '|') + CS_SpanEnd)) to sPath
        If (sWS = "") ;
            Function_Return (sPath + (((SpanOpen("dash-crumb-none")) + 'No workspace loaded') + CS_SpanEnd) + sTail + CS_DivEnd)
        Move (WorkspaceShortName(Self, sWS)) to sName
        /* THE FULL .sws PATH IS A TOOLTIP NOW, not a line of the bar (Nils 2026-08-22): "only the
           Editor view should show the full file name". Every screen carrying this crumb - both boards,
           Select Folders, Select Functions - printed the whole workspace path beside the short name.
           The Start Center was the only one without it, and only because it does not use this crumb.

           The path is not lost, it moved to where a path belongs: hover the workspace name. The bar
           shows the SHORT name, which is what identifies a workspace at a glance; the full path was
           answering a question nobody was asking, on four screens at once. */
        /* NAMED, not just shown (Nils 2026-08-22). A bold word after a separator is only obviously
           the workspace once you already know the bar; the label says what it is. It is deliberately
           the quiet half of the pair - the NAME is what the eye should land on, so the label takes the
           muted ink and the name keeps its weight. */
        Function_Return (sPath + (((SpanOpen("dash-crumb-lbl")) + 'Current Workspace:') + CS_SpanEnd + (SpanOpenTip("dash-crumb-name", sWS))) + sName + CS_SpanEnd + sTail + CS_DivEnd)
    End_Function

    // The crumb rooted at the START CENTER, with a tail slot - unchanged behaviour, and still what
    // any screen whose parent really is the Start Center should paint.
    Function WorkspaceCrumbTailHtml String sTail Returns String
        Function_Return (WorkspaceCrumbRootTailHtml(Self, (CrumbRootHtml(Self, False)), sTail))
    End_Function

    // ...and rooted at the surface the user actually came FROM - Select Folders and Select
    // Functions, the two screens reachable from the Start Center and from all three boards.
    Function WorkspaceCrumbSurfaceTailHtml String sTail Returns String
        Function_Return (WorkspaceCrumbRootTailHtml(Self, (CrumbRootHtml(Self, True)), sTail))
    End_Function

    // The plain crumb - what the two boards paint. Kept so neither had to change when the tail slot
    // was added; a screen with no next step should not have to say so.
    Function WorkspaceCrumbHtml Returns String
        Function_Return (WorkspaceCrumbTailHtml(Self, ""))
    End_Function

    // One metric's change vs the same-series prior entry: fewer (down) = teal improvement, more (up) =
    // coral regression, unchanged or no prior = a muted marker. Returned as an inline <i> chip. Defined
    // before ProgressTileHtml (its only caller) so the function-style call resolves at compile time.
    // Tooltips say "cycle", not "analyze" - a series is a program's compile laps OR the Deep Scan laps
    // (the reserved CS_ModProgressDeepScanLabel series), and the wording must fit both.
    Function ProgressDeltaHtml Integer iCur Integer iPrev Boolean bHavePrev Returns String
        Integer iDelta
        If (bHavePrev = False) ;
            Function_Return ('<i class="mp-d mp-flat" title="first recorded cycle for this series">' + CS_MidDot + '</i>')
        Move (iCur - iPrev) to iDelta
        If (iDelta < 0) ;
            Function_Return ('<i class="mp-d mp-down" title="' + String(iPrev - iCur) + (' fewer than the previous cycle">' + CS_DownTriangle) + String(iPrev - iCur) + '</i>')
        If (iDelta > 0) ;
            Function_Return ('<i class="mp-d mp-up" title="' + String(iDelta) + (' more than the previous cycle">' + CS_UpTriangle) + String(iDelta) + '</i>')
        Function_Return '<i class="mp-d mp-flat" title="unchanged from the previous cycle">0</i>'
    End_Function

    // How many analyzes the ModProgress history holds for ONE program = which CYCLE that program's
    // modernization is on (one snapshot is appended per analyze). The history interleaves programs,
    // so a raw row count would drift - count the matching rows. Shared by the Progress tile's foot
    // and the guided cycle strip so the two can never disagree. Called via Get (runtime dispatch).
    Function ModProgressCycleCount tModProgressFile Hist String sProg Returns Integer
        Integer i iN iCycle
        Move (SizeOfArray(Hist.aEntries)) to iN
        Move 0 to iCycle
        For i from 0 to (iN - 1)
            If (Hist.aEntries[i].sProgram = sProg) ;
                Increment iCycle
        Loop
        Function_Return iCycle
    End_Function

    // The modernization PROGRESS tile - a burn-down readout, DISTINCT from the Modernize tile it sits
    // below in the guided column (2026-07-09 guided-first redesign; it was a full-width strip below): that tile shows the
    // ABSOLUTE current counts and runs the plan; this shows the CHANGE (delta) vs the previous analyze
    // OF THE SAME PROGRAM, so errors / warnings / auto-fixes are seen falling across the Compile ->
    // Analyze -> Run cycles without having to recall the prior run's numbers. Fed by the per-workspace
    // history (ReadModProgress -> Data\ModProgress-<wskey>.json, one point per analyze appended in
    // cRefactorApplication.AppendModProgressEntry). RICH-TILE anatomy mirroring the Modernize tile
    // line-for-line (title / counts row / auto-fix row / History foot + the amber Guided badge) - a
    // matching four-line rich tile stacked in the guided column. A click anywhere opens the history modal (full table + trend + Reset); the badge
    // and the metric lines sit INSIDE the data-ServerOnClick carrier, so every click resolves to
    // "history" - a single-action tile needs no sibling isolation. Muted and INERT (no
    // data-ServerOnClick) until a workspace with at least one recorded analyze.
    /* ONE count in the progress tile: <span class="m-err"><b>7</b> errors<delta></span>. Four of
       these were written out on one line, each of them splitting <b> from </b> around the number,
       and the four differed only in class, field and noun. */
    Function _CountSpanHtml String sCls Integer iNow Integer iPrev Boolean bHavePrev String sLabel Returns String
        Function_Return ((SpanOpen(sCls)) + (BoldHtml(String(iNow))) + (" " + sLabel) ;
            + (ProgressDeltaHtml(Self, iNow, iPrev, bHavePrev)) + CS_SpanEnd)
    End_Function

    Function ProgressTileHtml Returns String
        String  sWS sBody sFoot sWhen sSeriesText
        tModProgressFile Hist
        tModProgressEntry Cur Prev
        Integer iN iLast iPrevIdx iCycle
        Boolean bHavePrev

        Get psSWSFile of ghoApplication to sWS
        If (sWS = "") ;
            Function_Return ((DivOpen("dash-readout dash-readout-m")) + (TileIcon((DashIcon(CS_GlyphTrend)))) + (DivOpen("dash-rtxt")) + (TileHeading("Modernization progress")) + (TileParagraph("Load a workspace to track its burn-down")) + (CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd))
        Get ReadModProgress of ghoApplication to Hist
        Move (SizeOfArray(Hist.aEntries)) to iN
        If (iN = 0) ;
            Function_Return ((DivOpen("dash-readout dash-readout-m")) + (TileIcon((DashIcon(CS_GlyphTrend)))) + (DivOpen("dash-rtxt")) + (TileHeading("Modernization progress")) + (TileParagraph("Run an analyze to start tracking the burn-down")) + (CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd))
        // Latest recorded analyze = the last entry; the delta compares it to the most recent PRIOR entry for
        // the SAME program (the file can interleave programs, so the previous ROW may be a different program -
        // comparing across programs would be meaningless). Scan backwards for the first same-program match.
        Move (iN - 1) to iLast
        Move Hist.aEntries[iLast] to Cur
        Move False to bHavePrev
        Move (iLast - 1) to iPrevIdx
        While (iPrevIdx >= 0 and bHavePrev = False)
            If (Hist.aEntries[iPrevIdx].sProgram = Cur.sProgram) Begin
                Move Hist.aEntries[iPrevIdx] to Prev
                Move True to bHavePrev
            End
            Decrement iPrevIdx
        Loop
        // Two-column redesign (2026-07-12): the Cycle count moved UP into this readout's header (it is a
        // burn-down concept), and this is now the SINGLE home for the figures - ONE counts row with the
        // stats (warnings / findings / errors / auto-fix / review - findings only on a cycle that has any,
        // see below), each trailing its delta vs the prior same-program analyze. Continue Modernizing above shows only the workspace roll-up, so no figure appears twice.
        // The whole readout carries data-ServerOnClick="history"; the Cycle pill is a plain styled span (no
        // own carrier) so a click on it bubbles to that single "history" action - no isolation needed.
        Get ModProgressCycleCount Hist Cur.sProgram to iCycle
        /* Series-aware FOOT wording (Nils 2026-07-16). Both laps are an "analyze" since 2026-08-10 -
           what differs is WHICH one, and sProgram is a STORED key, so the source series still says
           "Deep Scan" on disk and must be shown as CS_ModProgressScanSeriesText instead. */
        If (Cur.sProgram = CS_ModProgressDeepScanLabel) Begin
            Move "last source analyze" to sWhen
            Move CS_ModProgressScanSeriesText to sSeriesText
        End
        Else Begin
            Move "last analyze" to sWhen
            Move Cur.sProgram to sSeriesText
        End
        Move ((DivOpen("dash-prog-head")) + (TileHeading("Modernization progress")) + ((SpanOpen("dash-cyc-count")) + 'Cycle ') + String(iCycle) + (' &rsaquo;' + CS_SpanEnd + CS_DivEnd)) to sBody
        /* WARNINGS AND FINDINGS ARE TWO COUNTS (Nils 2026-09-15: "it would be better if that number
           is the actual number of warnings, not findings"). iWarn is the compiler's alone, so this
           now reads 0 after a source scan of a workspace that compiles clean - which is the truth,
           and the 796 it used to show sits on its own count beside it. The scan count appears only
           where a cycle has findings, so a plain compile lap's tile is unchanged; it appears when
           the PREVIOUS lap had them too, so the one cycle that cleared them still shows the fall.
           Same split, and the same rule for showing it, as the analyzer's chip bar. */
                Move (sBody + (DivOpen("dash-tile-counts")) ;
                    + (_CountSpanHtml(Self, "m-warn", Cur.iWarn, Prev.iWarn, bHavePrev, "warnings"))) to sBody
                If (Cur.iScan > 0 or Prev.iScan > 0) ;
                    Move (sBody + (_CountSpanHtml(Self, "m-scan", Cur.iScan, Prev.iScan, bHavePrev, "findings"))) to sBody
                Move (sBody ;
                    + (_CountSpanHtml(Self, "m-err",  Cur.iErr,     Prev.iErr,     bHavePrev, "errors")) ;
                    + (_CountSpanHtml(Self, "m-auto", Cur.iAuto,    Prev.iAuto,    bHavePrev, "auto-fix")) ;
                    + (_CountSpanHtml(Self, "m-rev",  Cur.iSuggest, Prev.iSuggest, bHavePrev, "review")) ;
                    + CS_DivEnd) to sBody
        Move (((DivOpen("dash-tile-foot")) + (SpanOpen("dash-tile-asof"))) + sSeriesText + ' ' + CS_MidDot + ' ' + sWhen + ' ' + Cur.sDate + (CS_SpanEnd + CS_DivEnd)) to sFoot
        Function_Return ((DivOpenClick("dash-readout dash-readout-m", CS_IdHistory, "", CS_ProgressTileTip)) + (TileIcon((DashIcon(CS_GlyphTrend)))) + (DivOpen("dash-rtxt")) + sBody + sFoot + (CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd))
    End_Function

    // One action-row chip. Enabled -> a clickable .dash-action carrying data-ServerOnClick=sId (the host maps
    // it to the deferred action) and the DOING tip (sTip). Disabled -> an inert .dash-action-off with NO
    // data-ServerOnClick, so a click resolves to nothing (the same gate model the path tiles use via their
    // psSWSFile OnClick guard) - and the ENABLING tip (sTipOff): a grey chip explains what lights it, the
    // same teach-the-pipeline model as the Test Compile strip (TestCompileFT's ActionChip).
    /* ONE CLICKABLE CHIP, for every board and dialog that builds one.

       Nils 2026-08-21, looking at the hand-written spans in DashboardFT: "it feels like we have
       css/html code scattered all over the place instead of using a more structured approach?" The
       markup itself cannot move to a file the way the stylesheets did - 79% of the HTML-building
       lines in that view interpolate a value, and DataFlex has no template engine to put a
       conditional or a loop in one. What CAN be shared is the SHAPE, and this is it.

       The gate model is the one the whole app already uses: enabled emits data-ServerOnClick, and
       disabled emits NO data-ServerOnClick at all, so a click on a dead chip resolves to nothing
       rather than to a handler that has to check whether it should have run.

       sClsOff is passed rather than derived because the two existing conventions disagree - the
       action row uses a separate class (dash-action-off) while the findings list uses a modifier
       (fact off). Deriving one would have quietly restyled whichever convention lost. */
    /* THE PRIMITIVE every clickable element in the app is built from.

       Only the TAG and the disabled-class convention ever differed between them: the boards and the
       findings list use <span> with an "off" modifier, the dialog bars use <div> with "dis". Both
       wrappers below pass their own, so neither convention had to move and nothing was restyled.

       The gate is the same everywhere: enabled emits data-ServerOnClick, disabled emits none at all,
       so a dead control resolves to nothing rather than to a handler that must ask whether it should
       have run. */

    /* A <div> button in a dialog bar - .rpbtn in the report bars, .sfbtn in the select bars, and the
       per-dialog classes (.tcbtn, .csbtn, .ml-btn ...) that buttons.css already styles as one family.

       The disabled class is "<cls> dis", which is what those bars use; the CSS for all of it has
       lived in buttons.css since the button sweep, so this is the markup half of a consolidation that
       was already half done. */

    /* The action-row chip, now a thin wrapper so its four callers keep working unchanged. It carries
       the one thing ChipHtml does not: a SEPARATE tooltip per state - the doing-tip when lit, the
       enabling-tip when grey, so a dead chip explains what would light it. */
    Function ActionChipHtml String sId String sLabel String sIcon String sTip String sTipOff Boolean bEnabled Returns String
        Function_Return (ChipHtml("dash-action", "dash-action-off", sId, "", ;
                                  (sIcon + sLabel), (If(bEnabled, sTip, sTipOff)), bEnabled))
    End_Function

    // Builds the bottom action-row tile: six verb chips (Run Modernization Plan / Run Refactoring / Read log / Read other logs /
    // Revert) mirroring the top-toolbar items of the same name. Each chip is GATED at render time with the
    // SAME signal that toolbar item's IsEnabled uses, all via ghoApplication (a global builder is outside the
    // app class, so app-scoped accessors must use ghoApplication, never Self). Each chip carries a per-STATE
    // tooltip: the doing-tip when lit, the enabling-tip when grey (CS_Act*OffTip; Run Refactoring
    // derives its grey tip DYNAMICALLY from whichever ingredient is missing). The chips are SIBLINGS in
    // a .dash-action-row wrapper that carries NO data-ServerOnClick, so each click resolves to exactly one id.
    // The actions are RUN from oDeferTimer.OnTimer (deferred off the web pump). The Undo gate is the costliest
    // (a recursive backup-folder walk); this builder runs only on refresh/load, never per click.
    Function ActionRowHtml Returns String
        String   sWS sHome sLogFile sHtml sStartOff sPlanOff
        Boolean  bStart bLog bOther bUndo bPlan bActionable
        Integer  iFolders iOther iUndo iFuncs
        String[] asOtherLogs
        tRFSearchResult[] BackupFiles

        // (1) Start: workspace loaded + functions selected + folders selected (oRefactor_ToolItem.IsEnabled).
        // Both counts are read up front (not short-circuited) so the DISABLED tip below can name the
        // SPECIFIC missing ingredient - the grey chip teaches the next click instead of just refusing.
        Get psSWSFile of ghoApplication to sWS
        Move 0 to iFuncs
        Move 0 to iFolders
        If (sWS <> "") Begin
            Move SysFile.SelectedFunctionTotal to iFuncs
            Get TotalSelectedFolders of (phoFolderSelHeaDD(ghoApplication)) to iFolders
        End
        Move (sWS <> "" and iFuncs > 0 and iFolders <> 0) to bStart
        Move CS_ActStartTip to sStartOff
        If (bStart = False) Begin
            If (sWS = "") ;
                Move "Load a workspace first - click the banner at the top." to sStartOff
            Else If (iFuncs = 0) ;
                Move "No refactoring functions are selected yet - open the function grid via a Manual-flow tile above (Single file or Workspace mode) and tick what to run." to sStartOff
            Else ;
                Move "No source folders are selected yet - click the folders pill on the Selected tile above to choose them." to sStartOff
        End
        // (2) Read log: the run summary log file exists on disk.
        Get psHomeTarget of ghoApplication to sHome
        Move (vFolderFormat(sHome)) to sHome
        Move (sHome + CS_BackupFolder + CS_DirSeparator + CS_SummaryLogfileName) to sLogFile
        Get vFilePathExists sLogFile to bLog
        // (3) Read other logs: any eOther_Function *.log.txt in the backup folder. iOther also labels the chip.
        Get OtherLogFiles of ghoApplication to asOtherLogs
        Move (SizeOfArray(asOtherLogs)) to iOther
        Move (iOther > 0) to bOther
        // (4) Revert/Undo: a backup set exists for this workspace (the recursive backup walk - costliest gate).
        // iUndo = the restorable backup-file count (AllBackupFolderFiles already drops the log/.bat artifacts).
        Get AllBackupFolderFiles of ghoApplication to BackupFiles
        Move (SizeOfArray(BackupFiles)) to iUndo
        Move (iUndo <> 0) to bUndo
        // (0) Run Modernization Plan: the saved-plan FILE exists on disk AND the last analyze had ACTIONABLE rows
        // (auto-fix/review) - the SAME two conditions the Modernize tile's "View last plan" link now uses, so a
        // plan whose .json was deleted, OR an empty analyze / a stale plan re-exposed by a revert, offers nothing
        // to run. (Nils 2026-07-07.) The grey tip names the specific blocker.
        Get SavedPlanFileExists of ghoApplication to bPlan
        Move ((ghiLastAnalyzeAuto + ghiLastAnalyzeSuggest) > 0) to bActionable
        If (bPlan = False) ;
            Move CS_ActPlanOffTip to sPlanOff
        Else ;
            Move "Nothing to run - the last analyze found no auto-fixable or review warnings to modernize (other programs in the workspace may still need it - analyze one that does)." to sPlanOff
        // Since the 2026-07-12 two-column redesign this strip holds ONLY the four after-a-run utilities;
        // the two run buttons moved into their flow columns (Run fix plan -> the guided diagram, Run
        // Refactoring -> the manual column, which reuse the bStart / bPlan / bActionable gates computed
        // above). The row is centred via .dash-action-row justify-content.
        Move (DivOpen("dash-action-row")) to sHtml
        Move (sHtml + (ActionChipHtml(Self, CS_IdReadLog,       "Read log",         (DashIcon(CS_GlyphFiletext)),  CS_ActLogTip,   CS_ActLogOffTip,   bLog)))   to sHtml
        Move (sHtml + (ActionChipHtml(Self, CS_IdReadOtherLogs, ("Read other logs (" + String(iOther) + ")"),  (DashIcon(CS_GlyphStack)), CS_ActOtherTip, CS_ActOtherOffTip, bOther))) to sHtml
        Move (sHtml + (ActionChipHtml(Self, CS_IdCompare,       "Compare Source",   (DashIcon(CS_GlyphCompare)), CS_ActCompareTip, CS_ActCompareOffTip, bUndo))) to sHtml
        Move (sHtml + (ActionChipHtml(Self, CS_IdUndo,          ("Revert (" + String(iUndo) + ")"),           (DashIcon(CS_GlyphUndo)),  CS_ActUndoTip,  CS_ActUndoOffTip,  bUndo)))  to sHtml
        Move (sHtml + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml
        Function_Return sHtml
    End_Function

    // Builds the Target-DataFlex-version tile HTML from ghoApplication: target version + compiler exe
    // basename + bitness, marked clickable (data-ServerOnClick="setup"). A pure builder (mirrors
    // the tile builders around it) so a second view could reuse the EXACT tile - one source of truth.
    Function SetupTileHtml Returns String
        String sVer sComp sCompBase sHtml sBits
        Integer iPos

        Get psTargetDfVersion of ghoApplication to sVer
        Get psCompiler        of ghoApplication to sComp
        Move (RightPos("\", sComp)) to iPos
        If (iPos > 0) ;
            Move (Right(sComp, (Length(sComp) - iPos))) to sCompBase
        Else ;
            Move sComp to sCompBase
        If (sVer = "") ;
            Move "-" to sVer
        If (sCompBase = "") ;
            Move "(not set)" to sCompBase
        // Bitness of the selected compiler, appended as a parenthetical after the exe name (blank when unknown).
        Get psCompilerBitness of ghoApplication to sBits
        If (sBits <> "") ;
            Move (" (" + sBits + ")") to sBits
        // REQUIRED-BUT-MISSING look (Nils 2026-07-17, the alpha-tester confusion): with no compiler
        // selected the tile trades its quiet gold for the WARNING skin + a pointed line, so the
        // missing setup is seen from the hub instead of discovered at the first compile. The
        // compile attempt itself also asks + opens the picker (TestCompileFT.StartCompile).
        /* ONE TILE, ONE SETTING (2026-09-10). Libraries used to be the right half of this tile,
           divided by a rule, on the reasoning that a library's verdict is a FUNCTION of the target
           version - change 25 to 26 and every verdict can flip, so the question belongs beside the
           input it depends on (Nils 2026-07-31). That reasoning still holds and is why the two are
           still adjacent, in that order, wearing the same gold; what changed is that a half of a
           half had no room left to say anything more. SetupLibsRowHtml below puts them side by side
           as siblings instead - see LibraryTileHtml in cFTLibraryReport.pkg.

           The click carrier came BACK onto the tile div with that move. It had been pushed down
           onto .dash-tgt-main because a cWebHtmlBox click fires every ancestor's ServerOnClick, so
           the nested Libraries chip would have opened Compiler Settings too. Nothing is nested here
           any more, so the tile carries its own action again. */
        If (sComp = "") ;
            Move (((DivOpenClick("dash-tile t-target t-target-warn", CS_IdSetup, "", CS_SetupTileTip)) + (TileIcon((DashIcon(CS_GlyphSettings)))) + (DivOpen("dash-txt")) + (TileHeading("Target DataFlex version")) + ((DivOpen("dash-p")) + ((BoldText("No compiler selected")) + ' ')) + CS_EmDash + (' click to choose' + CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd))) to sHtml
        Else ;
            Move (((DivOpenClick("dash-tile t-target", CS_IdSetup, "", CS_SetupTileTip)) + (TileIcon((DashIcon(CS_GlyphSettings)))) + (DivOpen("dash-txt")) + (TileHeading("Target DataFlex version")) + ((DivOpen("dash-p")) + 'DataFlex ') + sVer + ' ' + CS_MidDot + ' ' + sCompBase + sBits + (CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd))) to sHtml
        Function_Return sHtml
    End_Function

    /* THE HEADER ROW, shared since the Manual board wanted it too (2026-08-02).

       Target DataFlex version, Libraries and Function library as flex children of one .dash-cols
       host tile - separate span-6 tiles do not level their heights, which is why they share a host
       at all (the full story is in application.css).

       CountFnGroup walks the Functions table, so this half is only meaningful once the startup
       function-sync has run - the same condition the Dashboard always had. It reads the globally
       declared table, so it moves here without dragging a view along.
    */
    // Counts the library's PUBLISHED refactoring functions by FnGroup (reads the globally-declared Functions
    // table; the Find loop disturbs the Functions buffer - harmless for a read-only dashboard). The bPublished=1
    // guard is essential: the Functions table also holds UNpublished rows - config records (the editor tab-size,
    // CountSourceLines, ...) and any functions removed from the code - which carry FnGroup=0 and would otherwise
    // inflate "Other", so the group counts no longer sum to the real function total. Mirrors the canonical
    // cFunctionsDataDictionary.TotalNoOfFunctions, which also constrains on bPublished.
    Function CountFnGroup Integer eGroup Returns Integer
        Integer iCount
        Move 0 to iCount
        Clear Functions
        Find GT Functions by 1
        While (Found)
            If ((Functions.FnGroup = eGroup) and (Functions.bPublished = 1)) ;
                Increment iCount
            Find GT Functions by 1
        Loop
        Function_Return iCount
    End_Function
    /* ONE clickable count in the function-library row. Five of these were written out as five raw
       spans on a single 900-character line - open tag, click id, tooltip, <b>, count, label, close,
       five times over, with the concatenation groups falling wherever they happened to land.

       SpanOpenClick emits the identical bytes (blank param drops data-OnClickParam, the tip is not
       escaped), and BoldText wraps the count - escaping digits is a no-op, so the output is
       unchanged. */
    Function _FnCountHtml String sCls String sId Integer iCount String sLabel String sTip Returns String
        Function_Return ((SpanOpenClick(sCls, sId, "", sTip)) + (BoldText(String(iCount))) + ' ' + sLabel + CS_SpanEnd)
    End_Function

    // The function-library card (FnGroup counts). Was built inline by RefreshStats; it is a function now
    // because the paired row has to rebuild BOTH halves in one UpdateHtml. Reads the Functions table, so
    // it is only meaningful once the startup function-sync has run.
    Function StatsCardHtml Returns String
        Integer iMod iU64 iClean iOther iTotal
        String  sHtml

        Move (CountFnGroup(Self, eFnGroupModernization)) to iMod
        Move (CountFnGroup(Self, eFnGroupUnicode64))     to iU64
        Move (CountFnGroup(Self, eFnGroupCleanup))       to iClean
        Move (CountFnGroup(Self, eFnGroupOther))         to iOther
        Move (iMod + iU64 + iClean + iOther) to iTotal

        Move ((DivOpenTip("dash-stat", CS_StatsTileTip)) ;
            + (DivOpenClick("dash-label dash-fnbtn", CS_IdFnLib, "", "")) ;
            + (DashIcon(CS_GlyphStack)) + 'Function library' + CS_DivEnd ;
            + (DivOpen("dash-row")) ;
            + (_FnCountHtml(Self, "dash-total dash-fnbtn", "fnlib",      iTotal, "Total",         "Open the function library - all groups")) ;
            + (_FnCountHtml(Self, "dash-mod dash-fnbtn",   "fnlibmod",   iMod,   "Modernization", "Show only the Modernization functions")) ;
            + (_FnCountHtml(Self, "dash-u64 dash-fnbtn",   "fnlibu64",   iU64,   "x64 + Unicode", "Show only the x64 + Unicode functions")) ;
            + (_FnCountHtml(Self, "dash-clean dash-fnbtn", "fnlibtidy",  iClean, "Tidy Up",       "Show only the Tidy Up functions")) ;
            + (_FnCountHtml(Self, "dash-other dash-fnbtn", "fnlibother", iOther, "Other",         "Show only the Other functions")) ;
            + CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml

        Function_Return sHtml
    End_Function
    /* THE HEADER ROW, in ONE host tile as flex children of .dash-cols - the same trick the
       Guided | Manual columns use, and for the same reason. Separate span-6 tiles do NOT level: the
       host sizes each control to its own content, so a row of them only ever LOOKS equal while every
       tile happens to hit its min-height floor. The Setup tile grew a Libraries half, outgrew the
       floor, and the row went crooked (Nils 2026-08-01: "could the Function library tile be made the
       same height"). align-items:stretch makes it real rather than coincidental, whatever any of them
       ends up holding - and it is what made splitting Libraries out into its own tile safe on
       2026-09-10, which it would not have been while two sibling tiles could not level.

       THE GAP NEEDS NO RULE: every card already carries margin 6px from the shared card shape, so
       siblings in this row sit 12px apart. A flex gap here would also space the Guided | Manual
       columns, which carry their own margins and do not want it.

       Setup and Libraries are the SHARED pair (the trail paints them too, via SetupLibsRowHtml); the
       stats tile is this board's alone - the trail has no function-library tile. */
    Function SetupStatsRowHtml Returns String
        // Self for the two tiles this class builds; Libraries builds its own from the data object that
        // already owns those counts. This wrapper used to live in the view and reach out to
        // ghoTileMarkup; inside the class that global is not declared until after End_Class - and Self
        // is what it means anyway. (Moved here 2026-08-02 for the Manual board.)
        Function_Return ((DivOpen("dash-cols")) + (SetupTileHtml(Self)) + (LibraryTileHtml(ghoLibraryReport)) + (StatsCardHtml(Self)) + CS_DivEnd)
    End_Function
    /* The same row WITHOUT the function-library tile, for the guided trail - it has no such tile, and
       painting Target alone would drop Libraries off that board entirely. That is what the split would
       otherwise have done silently: the trail got Libraries for free while it was nested inside Setup. */
    Function SetupLibsRowHtml Returns String
        Function_Return ((DivOpen("dash-cols")) + (SetupTileHtml(Self)) + (LibraryTileHtml(ghoLibraryReport)) + CS_DivEnd)
    End_Function
    // Design-time seed for that row: every tile in its workspace-off state, so the FIRST paint has them
    // already side by side (no WebView2-mount race) and no placeholder carries a click carrier.
    // RefreshSetup / RefreshStats replace the whole row once a workspace is loaded. Tips are the live
    // ones where a constant exists; Libraries states its off-condition instead, because that tile's
    // live tooltip describes a verdict this placeholder has not got.
    Function HeaderSeedHtml Returns String
        Function_Return (((DivOpen("dash-cols")) + (DivOpenTip("dash-tile-off", CS_SetupTileTip))) + (TileIcon((DashIcon(CS_GlyphSettings)))) + (DivOpen("dash-txt")) + (TileHeading("Target DataFlex version")) + (TileParagraph("Load a workspace to see the target")) + (CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd + (DivOpenTip("dash-tile-off", "The shared libraries this workspace uses - load a workspace to see them."))) + (TileIcon((DashIcon(CS_GlyphStack)))) + (DivOpen("dash-txt")) + (TileHeading("Libraries")) + (TileParagraph("Load a workspace to see them")) + (CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd + (DivOpenTip("dash-stat-off", CS_StatsTileTip))) + (DivOpen("dash-label")) + (DashIcon(CS_GlyphStack)) + ('Function library' + CS_DivEnd) + (TileParagraph("Load a workspace to see counts")) + (CS_DivEnd + CS_DivEnd))
    End_Function

End_Class

// One instance. The Dashboard and the guided trail both paint their tiles through this handle.
#IFNDEF ghoTileMarkup
    Global_Variable Handle ghoTileMarkup
    Move 0 to ghoTileMarkup
#ENDIF

Object oTileMarkup is a cFTTileMarkup
    Move Self to ghoTileMarkup
End_Object
